{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 160,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can I hold it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2880,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only if you promise to be really, really careful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5870,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I promise I will be so incredibly careful.\nI will be incredibly careful with it. I promise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13730,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, it's slippery, be careful.\nAlright, are we ready?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22500,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm about to touch a 1kg sphere of silicon-28\natoms. There are about 2.15x10^25 of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36149,
    "dDurationMs": 5461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It feels absolutely incredible. Wow, that\nis amazing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41610,
    "dDurationMs": 5679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Besides its creators, I am one of only a handful\nof people ever to hold this sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47289,
    "dDurationMs": 5011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The raw material used to make it was worth\n1 million Euros but now that it has been so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52300,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "precisely sculpted --"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53940,
    "dDurationMs": 2259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How much is that worth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56199,
    "dDurationMs": 6171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's priceless. ... This you are looking at\nnow is the roundest object in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62370,
    "dDurationMs": 5330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How can you say for sure it's the roundest\nobject? I mean the Earth is pretty round,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67700,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't it?\nIf this was the Earth..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69470,
    "dDurationMs": 6990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this were the Earth then the highest mountain\nto the lowest valley would be... about 14m"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76460,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78690,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is shocking. That is shockingly round."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82560,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why would you invest one million Euros\nand thousands of man-hours perfecting a pure,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88280,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "polished silicon sphere?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91010,
    "dDurationMs": 6820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the answer is grave. Or rather 'grave'\nas it would have been pronounced in the original"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97830,
    "dDurationMs": 310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "French."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98140,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see the grave was the original name for\nthe base unit of mass in the metric system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103070,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which became the Systeme International d'unites\nor SI units. In 1793, a commision which included"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109950,
    "dDurationMs": 6270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "notable scientist and aristocrat Antoine Lavoisier,\ndefined the base unit of mass as the weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116220,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a cubic decimeter of water at the melting\ntemperature of ice -- essentially just a litre"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121740,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of ice water. The name grave came from the\nLatin gravitas, meaning weight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127040,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it wasn't to last. It sounded too similar\nto the aristocratic title 'graf' -- which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132420,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the equivalent of an earl or a count. And\nwith the French revolution in full swing with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137640,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rallying cry of equality for all, you\ncouldn't exactly have one unit nobler than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143060,
    "dDurationMs": 6710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the others. At this Lavoisier lost his head,\nliterally, not because he helped devise one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149770,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the greatest systems of measurement of\nall time, but because he was collecting taxes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153880,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a nobleman."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155560,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So things really were grave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157670,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The new republican government believed a grave\nwould be too big for the things they wanted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161470,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to measure anyway and and so they settled\non the gramme, which was just a thousandth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165810,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the grave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167280,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But soon they realized that a gram was too\nsmall and so they returned to the grave, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171480,
    "dDurationMs": 6170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since they couldn't call it that, they invented\nthe kilogram -- a thousand grams. And that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177650,
    "dDurationMs": 5860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is why out of the seven base SI units, the\nkilogram is the only one to have a prefix"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183510,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in its name."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184960,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1799 the kilogram definition was refined\nto be the mass of a litre of water at 4 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190960,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Celcius -- the temperature at which it is\ndensest. But water itself is obviously not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196180,
    "dDurationMs": 6450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most sensible thing to use as a mass standard.\nSo a pure platinum cylinder was created to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202630,
    "dDurationMs": 6439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the same mass as the water definition\nand it was declared Kilogram of the Archives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209069,
    "dDurationMs": 4611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now it's important to note at this point the\nkilogram is no longer tied to the mass of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a volume of water -- the kilogram of the archives\nis by definition THE kilogram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219200,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "90 years later, in 1889 the kilogram was upgraded\nto a platinum-iridium alloy cylinder. Now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226810,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was much harder than the original but was\notherwise basically identical. And to this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231850,
    "dDurationMs": 6370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "day, it remains the definition of the kilogram.\nIt is officially called the International"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238220,
    "dDurationMs": 6849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Prototype Kilogram, though it's affectionately\nknown as Le Grand K -- or Big K. Oh, and it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245069,
    "dDurationMs": 1361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about this big..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246430,
    "dDurationMs": 6610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the only thing in the entire universe\nwith a mass of exactly one kilogram because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253040,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it IS the kilogram. It is also the only SI\nunit that is still defined by a physical object."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260870,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It sits under three bell jars, next to six\nsister kilograms, in a climate-controlled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266530,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vault locked by three independently controlled\nkeys, in the basement of the International"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271500,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bureau of Weights and Measures on the outskirts\nof Paris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275100,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you were able to break into the vault\nand tamper with Big K, you would be changing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280500,
    "dDurationMs": 5470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the definition of the kilogram, a definition\non which many of our measurements rely, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285970,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you would throw the world into chaos! Well\nno, not actually-- but how would anyone ever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292930,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know if the mass of Big K changed?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296630,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well when it was first created, 40 identical\nreplicas were also made. Well they weren't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301910,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quite identical - they had a mass which was\nslightly different to Big K but those offsets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306990,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were recorded. Now these replicas were sent\nout to countries around the world to serve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311490,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as their national standards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312750,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1948 the kilograms were reunited for a\nweigh-in. And this is when the problems started."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320330,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because even though all the cylinders were\nmade of the same alloy and stored under virtually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324930,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same conditions, their masses had diverged\nover time. The mass of Big K wasn't even the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331650,
    "dDurationMs": 5049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same as the six sister cylinders stored with\nit. And to make matters worse when they were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336699,
    "dDurationMs": 5291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brought together again forty years later,\ntheir masses had further diverged, up to about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341990,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "50 micrograms - that's about the weight of\na fingerprint. But fingerprints were not the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347190,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "culprits since the kilograms were carefully\nwashed before their weigh-ins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351100,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So some physical process must have actually\nchanged the mass of the cylinders, but how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357300,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that exactly works remains a matter of speculation.\nOne this is for certain, the mass of a platinum-iridium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364530,
    "dDurationMs": 5790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cylinder is not stable over time. And this\nis a big problem. You can't have a unit which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370320,
    "dDurationMs": 3470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changes its value.\nAnd the fallout isn't limited to measurements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373790,
    "dDurationMs": 6750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of mass since of the seven base SI units,\nfour of them depend on the mass of the kilogram,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380540,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not to mention all the derived units like\nNewtons, Joules, Volts and Watts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385320,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this point those of you in countries that\nhave not adopted the metric system--yes I'm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389680,
    "dDurationMs": 6269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speaking to you Liberia, Burma, and the US--you\nmay be feeling rather smug that your unit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395949,
    "dDurationMs": 6651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of mass, the avoirdupois pound, is no longer\ndefined by a physical object. No, instead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402600,
    "dDurationMs": 5410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is defined as precisely 0.45359237"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408010,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kilograms. Sucked in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412870,
    "dDurationMs": 5930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So clearly something needs to be done to eliminate\nthe kilogram's dependence on a physical object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is where the silicon sphere comes\nin, but how exactly does that help?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here you have a physical object and it's beautiful\nbut you know it's still a physical object."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429120,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're trying to get away from that.\nWe're trying to get away from the physical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431990,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "object but what we're doing with this particular\nobject is counting how many atoms are in there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439990,
    "dDurationMs": 2519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't actually count how many are in there\ncan you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442509,
    "dDurationMs": 3871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't count how many are in there but\nyou can calculate how many are in there because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446380,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this material is silicon, there's no voids\nor dislocations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450470,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is like a perfect crystal of silicon.\nThat's right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454259,
    "dDurationMs": 6391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only is it pure silicon, it contains only\none isotope of silicon, silicon-28, and that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460650,
    "dDurationMs": 2739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explains why the original material was so\nexpensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463389,
    "dDurationMs": 6211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And why a sphere?\nWell, a sphere is a pretty simple object."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you know the diameter of the sphere you\ncan characterise the entire dimension of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474400,
    "dDurationMs": 2530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "object.\nWell that explains why the sphere has to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476930,
    "dDurationMs": 5799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the roundest object ever created, but how\ndo you actually make something that round?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482729,
    "dDurationMs": 6011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We actually start with an oversized sphere.\nSo it was about two millimetres larger in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488740,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "diameter and then we just grind it progressively\nfiner and finer using abrasive. It's actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496250,
    "dDurationMs": 5199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "massaging atoms. You're down at that level\nof trying to control the shape of an object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501449,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down at the atomic level.\nBut making the sphere is only half the battle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505889,
    "dDurationMs": 5941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you need to accurately measure its diameter.\nThe diameter is actually measured via a laser."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511830,
    "dDurationMs": 5449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you're actually measuring having the sphere\nin the centre of a cavity and a laser is hitting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517279,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both sides and you're actually measuring the\ngap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519759,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By knowing the diameter you can determine\nits volume. And since the atom spacing in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524139,
    "dDurationMs": 5461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "silicon is known to high precision, you can\nthe calculate how many atoms make up the sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529600,
    "dDurationMs": 6159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This allows you to redefine Avogadro's constant.\nAt the moment, Avogadro's constant is defined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535759,
    "dDurationMs": 5281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "based on the kilogram. It is equal to the\nnumber of atoms in twelve grams of carbon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541040,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "12. But using this approach, the number of\nsilicon atoms in the sphere would be used"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545980,
    "dDurationMs": 4709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fix Avogadro's constant, which would then\ndefine the kilogram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550689,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even if the silicon spheres were lost or\ndamaged, it would have no effect on the definition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555819,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the kilogram because it would be defined\nnot by a physical object but by a concept."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560679,
    "dDurationMs": 5861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You would like to see the official definition\nof the kilogram say \"a kilogram is the mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566540,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 2.15x10^25 silicon-28 atoms\"\nYes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570339,
    "dDurationMs": 6670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it - is it going to happen?\nThere's a likelihood, a high likelihood that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577009,
    "dDurationMs": 2781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's going to happen.\nBut there is another approach to redefining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579790,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the kilogram which involves fixing Planck's\nconstant and it's done using something called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585290,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Watt Balance. These two approaches are complimentary.\nEach one provides a check on the other, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592369,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if they show good agreement and are able to\nbring their uncertainties down to about twenty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596490,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "micrograms they may redefine the kilogram\nas early as 2014. And then the kilogram finally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603679,
    "dDurationMs": 6301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will be an unchanging unit, no longer defined\nby a physical object in the basement vault"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609980,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of some place in Paris.\nNow if the kilogram was originally intended"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629639,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be the mass of a litre of water at its\ndensest temperature then how well did we do?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636139,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well if you look at a litre of water at nearly\nfour degrees Celcius it has a mass of 999.975"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643929,
    "dDurationMs": 6780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grams. So I guess you could look at this two\nways. On the one hand you could say the kilogram"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650709,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is slightly heavier than it should be, but\non the other hand 214 years ago, scientists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657389,
    "dDurationMs": 6781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were able to create an artifact that was correct\nwithin the margin of error of a grain of rice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664170,
    "dDurationMs": 5779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that is truly remarkable. Now if you want\nto hear more about the Watt Balance, let me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669949,
    "dDurationMs": 4401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know in the comments and I will see what I\ncan do. It does seem to be the frontrunner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674350,
    "dDurationMs": 5979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in terms of redefining the kilogram, so we\nwill have to wait and see what happens. One"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680329,
    "dDurationMs": 4151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "last thing, I should point out that it took\nan international collaboration of scientists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684480,
    "dDurationMs": 4729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to create the silicon sphere but don't you\nthink that the scientist who originally conceived"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689209,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of silicon as an element should receive some\nof the credit. Well in 1787, that was none"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694529,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other than Antoine Lavoisier. So he's been\ninvolved in the definition of a kilogram from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699069,
    "dDurationMs": 2991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "start to finish or from cradle to grave."
    } ]
  } ]
}
